---
import Layout from '../../../../layouts/Layout.astro';

const lessons = [
  {
    number: 1,
    title: "Hello, NES World",
    description: "Initialize the hardware and display a solid colour background using 6502 assembly.",
    status: "available"
  }
];
---

<Layout
  title="Tier 1: Discovery - Phase 1 - Nintendo Entertainment System"
  description="Learn NES programming in 6502 assembly. Master PPU initialization, background colours, and ROM structure. Build your first working NES program that displays on real hardware."
>
  <style>
    .course-hero {
      background: linear-gradient(135deg, #e30613 0%, #ff6b6b 100%);
      color: white;
      padding: var(--space-12) var(--space-4);
      text-align: center;
      margin-bottom: var(--space-12);
    }

    .course-title {
      font-family: var(--font-family-mono);
      font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3rem);
      font-weight: 900;
      margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
      text-shadow: 2px 2px 4px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.3);
    }

    .course-subtitle {
      font-size: 1.25rem;
      opacity: 0.95;
      margin-bottom: var(--space-6);
    }

    .course-description {
      max-width: 700px;
      margin: 0 auto var(--space-8);
      font-size: 1.125rem;
      line-height: 1.7;
      opacity: 0.95;
    }

    .course-stats {
      display: flex;
      gap: var(--space-8);
      justify-content: center;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
    }

    .stat-item {
      text-align: center;
    }

    .stat-value {
      font-size: 2rem;
      font-weight: bold;
      font-family: var(--font-family-mono);
    }

    .stat-label {
      font-size: 0.875rem;
      opacity: 0.9;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      letter-spacing: 0.05em;
    }

    .content-container {
      max-width: 1000px;
      margin: 0 auto;
      padding: 0 var(--space-4);
    }

    .section-title {
      font-size: 2rem;
      margin-bottom: var(--space-6);
      color: var(--color-text);
    }

    .intro-section {
      background: var(--color-surface);
      border: 2px solid #e30613;
      border-radius: 0.75rem;
      padding: var(--space-8);
      margin-bottom: var(--space-12);
    }

    .intro-section h2 {
      color: #e30613;
      margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
      font-size: 1.5rem;
    }

    .intro-section p {
      color: var(--color-text-secondary);
      line-height: 1.7;
      margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
    }

    .intro-section ul {
      color: var(--color-text-secondary);
      line-height: 1.7;
      padding-left: var(--space-6);
    }

    .intro-section li {
      margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
    }

    .lessons-grid {
      display: grid;
      gap: var(--space-4);
      margin-bottom: var(--space-12);
    }

    .lesson-card {
      background: var(--color-surface);
      border: 2px solid var(--color-border);
      border-radius: 0.75rem;
      padding: var(--space-6);
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: auto 1fr auto;
      gap: var(--space-4);
      align-items: center;
      text-decoration: none;
      color: var(--color-text);
      transition: all var(--transition-base);
    }

    .lesson-card:hover {
      border-color: #e30613;
      transform: translateX(4px);
      box-shadow: 0 4px 12px rgba(227, 6, 19, 0.1);
    }

    .lesson-number {
      width: 50px;
      height: 50px;
      background: linear-gradient(135deg, #e30613 0%, #ff6b6b 100%);
      color: white;
      border-radius: 50%;
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      justify-content: center;
      font-family: var(--font-family-mono);
      font-size: 1.25rem;
      font-weight: bold;
    }

    .lesson-content {
      flex: 1;
    }

    .lesson-title {
      font-size: 1.25rem;
      font-weight: 600;
      margin-bottom: var(--space-1);
      color: var(--color-text);
    }

    .lesson-description {
      color: var(--color-text-secondary);
      font-size: 0.9rem;
      line-height: 1.5;
    }

    .lesson-status {
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      gap: var(--space-2);
      font-size: 0.875rem;
      font-weight: 500;
      padding: var(--space-2) var(--space-3);
      border-radius: 9999px;
      background: rgba(227, 6, 19, 0.1);
      color: #e30613;
    }

    .start-button {
      display: inline-block;
      padding: var(--space-4) var(--space-8);
      background: linear-gradient(135deg, #e30613 0%, #ff6b6b 100%);
      color: white;
      font-size: 1.125rem;
      font-weight: 600;
      text-decoration: none;
      border-radius: 0.5rem;
      transition: all var(--transition-base);
    }

    .start-button:hover {
      transform: translateY(-2px);
      box-shadow: 0 8px 20px rgba(227, 6, 19, 0.3);
    }

    .wow-box {
      background: var(--color-bg);
      border-left: 4px solid #e30613;
      padding: var(--space-4);
      margin: var(--space-6) 0;
      border-radius: 0 0.5rem 0.5rem 0;
    }

    .wow-box strong {
      color: #e30613;
      font-family: var(--font-family-mono);
    }

    .back-link {
      display: inline-flex;
      align-items: center;
      gap: var(--space-2);
      color: var(--color-text-secondary);
      text-decoration: none;
      margin-bottom: var(--space-8);
    }

    .back-link:hover {
      color: var(--color-text);
    }

    .wip-notice {
      background: #fff3cd;
      border: 2px solid #ffc107;
      border-radius: 0.75rem;
      padding: var(--space-6);
      margin-bottom: var(--space-8);
      color: #856404;
    }

    .wip-notice h3 {
      color: #856404;
      margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
      font-size: 1.25rem;
    }

    @media (max-width: 768px) {
      .lesson-card {
        grid-template-columns: 1fr;
        text-align: center;
      }

      .lesson-number {
        margin: 0 auto;
      }

      .lesson-status {
        justify-self: center;
      }
    }
  </style>

  <!-- Course Hero -->
  <section class="course-hero">
    <h1 class="course-title">TIER 1: DISCOVERY</h1>
    <p class="course-subtitle">Phase 1 - Assembly Foundation</p>

    <p class="course-description">
      The NES has no built-in BASIC—you write assembly code that talks directly to the hardware. Learn how to initialize the PPU, set background colours, and create a working ROM that runs on real hardware. Master the iNES format, VBlank timing, and 6502 instructions.
    </p>

    <div class="course-stats">
      <div class="stat-item">
        <div class="stat-value">1</div>
        <div class="stat-label">Lesson (So Far)</div>
      </div>
      <div class="stat-item">
        <div class="stat-value">15–25</div>
        <div class="stat-label">Minutes Each</div>
      </div>
      <div class="stat-item">
        <div class="stat-value">6502</div>
        <div class="stat-label">Assembly</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Course Introduction -->
  <div class="content-container">
    <a href="/nintendo-entertainment-system/phase-1" class="back-link">
      ← Back to Phase 1
    </a>

    <div class="wip-notice">
      <h3>🚧 Work In Progress</h3>
      <p>
        NES lessons are being added incrementally. More lessons coming soon! Each lesson includes working code you can assemble and run on FCEUX, Mesen, or real hardware via flash cart.
      </p>
    </div>

    <section class="intro-section">
      <h2>What You'll Learn This Tier</h2>

      <p>
        Tier 1 introduces NES programming from first principles. Unlike the C64 or Spectrum, the NES has no BASIC interpreter—you write assembly code that runs directly on the 6502 CPU. These lessons teach:
      </p>

      <ul>
        <li><strong>iNES ROM Format:</strong> Magic header, PRG-ROM, CHR-ROM, mapper configuration</li>
        <li><strong>6502 Assembly Basics:</strong> SEI, CLD, LDA, STA, BIT, BPL, JMP, RTI instructions</li>
        <li><strong>PPU Initialization:</strong> Waiting for VBlank, reading PPUSTATUS ($2002)</li>
        <li><strong>Palette RAM:</strong> Writing to $3F00 via PPUADDR ($2006) and PPUDATA ($2007)</li>
        <li><strong>Background Rendering:</strong> Enabling display via PPUMASK ($2001)</li>
        <li><strong>Interrupt Vectors:</strong> NMI ($FFFA), Reset ($FFFC), IRQ ($FFFE)</li>
      </ul>

      <div class="wow-box">
        <strong>Tier 1 Goal:</strong> Build a working NES ROM that displays on screen. You'll master the minimal initialization sequence every NES game must perform, understand how the PPU memory map works, and create ROMs you can run on real hardware.
      </div>

      <p>
        <strong>Prerequisites:</strong> Basic understanding of hexadecimal and binary. Experience with any assembly language helpful but not required. You'll need ca65/ld65 (from cc65 suite) and an NES emulator like FCEUX or Mesen.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- Lessons List -->
    <section>
      <h2 class="section-title">Lessons</h2>

      <div class="lessons-grid">
        {lessons.map(lesson => (
          <a href={`/nintendo-entertainment-system/phase-1/tier-1/lesson-${String(lesson.number).padStart(3, '0')}`}
             class="lesson-card">
            <div class="lesson-number">{lesson.number}</div>
            <div class="lesson-content">
              <h3 class="lesson-title">{lesson.title}</h3>
              <p class="lesson-description">{lesson.description}</p>
            </div>
            <div class="lesson-status">Start →</div>
          </a>
        ))}
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Call to Action -->
    <section style="text-align: center; margin: var(--space-16) 0;">
      <h2 class="section-title">Ready to Start?</h2>
      <p style="color: var(--color-text-secondary); margin-bottom: var(--space-4); max-width: 600px; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;">
        Install ca65/ld65, boot your emulator, and let's write your first NES ROM!
      </p>
      <a href="/nintendo-entertainment-system/phase-1/tier-1/lesson-001" class="start-button">
        Start Lesson 1: Hello, NES World
      </a>
    </section>
  </div>
</Layout>
